{"id": "lunyu-2-12", "work": "论语", "chapter": "为政", "ref": "2.12", "original": "子曰：“君子不器。”", "gloss": "人的价值不能被某一种固定用途框住，不能像器具那样只派一个用场。", "theme": ["自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E7%88%B2%E6%94%BF%E7%AC%AC%E4%BA%8C?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·为政》2.12", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "lunyu-2-17", "work": "论语", "chapter": "为政", "ref": "2.17", "original": "子曰：“由，诲女知之乎！知之为知之，不知为不知，是知也。”", "gloss": "知道就承认知道，不知道就承认不知道，这才是真正的明白。", "theme": ["自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E7%88%B2%E6%94%BF%E7%AC%AC%E4%BA%8C?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·为政》2.17", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "lunyu-4-08", "work": "论语", "chapter": "里仁", "ref": "4.8", "original": "子曰：“朝闻道，夕死可矣！”", "gloss": "如果早晨真正明白了自己该走的路，即使当晚死去，这一生也不算白活。", "theme": ["意义与虚无"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E9%87%8C%E4%BB%81%E7%AC%AC%E5%9B%9B?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·里仁》4.8", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "lunyu-4-09", "work": "论语", "chapter": "里仁", "ref": "4.9", "original": "子曰：“士志于道，而耻恶衣恶食者，未足与议也！”", "gloss": "一个人立志求道，却因为穿得差、吃得差而羞耻，那就不值得再和他谈什么道了。", "theme": ["金钱与安全"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E9%87%8C%E4%BB%81%E7%AC%AC%E5%9B%9B?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·里仁》4.9", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "lunyu-4-17", "work": "论语", "chapter": "里仁", "ref": "4.17", "original": "子曰：“见贤思齐焉，见不贤而内自省也。”", "gloss": "看到比自己好的人就想赶上他，看到做得不好的人就回头检查自己有没有同样的毛病。", "theme": ["自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E9%87%8C%E4%BB%81%E7%AC%AC%E5%9B%9B?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·里仁》4.17", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "lunyu-9-17", "work": "论语", "chapter": "子罕", "ref": "9.17", "original": "子在川上曰：“逝者如斯夫！不舍昼夜。”", "gloss": "时间就像这条河，日夜不停地流走，不会为任何人停下。", "theme": ["时间与消耗"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E5%AD%90%E7%BD%95%E7%AC%AC%E4%B9%9D?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·子罕》9.17", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "lunyu-9-23", "work": "论语", "chapter": "子罕", "ref": "9.23", "original": "子曰：“后生可畏，焉知来者之不如今也？四十、五十而无闻焉，斯亦不足畏也已！”", "gloss": "年轻人值得敬畏，怎么知道后来者不如现在的人？但人到了四五十岁还没有值得称道的东西，也就不再值得敬畏了。", "theme": ["时间与消耗", "失败与脆弱"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E5%AD%90%E7%BD%95%E7%AC%AC%E4%B9%9D?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·子罕》9.23", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "lunyu-9-26", "work": "论语", "chapter": "子罕", "ref": "9.26", "original": "子曰：“三军可夺帅也，匹夫不可夺志也。”", "gloss": "一支军队可以被夺走主帅，一个普通人的志向却不能被别人夺走。", "theme": ["自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E5%AD%90%E7%BD%95%E7%AC%AC%E4%B9%9D?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·子罕》9.26", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "lunyu-9-28", "work": "论语", "chapter": "子罕", "ref": "9.28", "original": "子曰：“岁寒，然后知松柏之后凋也。”", "gloss": "到了天寒地冻的时候，才看得出松柏是最后凋零的——困境才照出谁真正撑得住。", "theme": ["失败与脆弱"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E5%AD%90%E7%BD%95%E7%AC%AC%E4%B9%9D?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·子罕》9.28", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "lunyu-9-29", "work": "论语", "chapter": "子罕", "ref": "9.29", "original": "子曰：“知者不惑，仁者不忧，勇者不惧。”", "gloss": "有智慧的人不迷惑，有仁德的人不忧愁，有勇气的人不畏惧。", "theme": ["恐惧与焦虑"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E5%AD%90%E7%BD%95%E7%AC%AC%E4%B9%9D?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·子罕》9.29", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "lunyu-15-23", "work": "论语", "chapter": "卫灵公", "ref": "15.23", "original": "子贡问曰：“有一言而可以终身行之者乎？”子曰：“其恕乎！己所不欲，勿施于人。”", "gloss": "自己不愿意承受的事，就不要加到别人身上。", "theme": ["关系与冲突"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E8%A1%9E%E9%9D%88%E5%85%AC%E7%AC%AC%E5%8D%81%E4%BA%94?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·卫灵公》15.23", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "lunyu-15-29", "work": "论语", "chapter": "卫灵公", "ref": "15.29", "original": "子曰：“过而不改，是谓过矣。”", "gloss": "犯了错却不肯改，这个错才真正成了错。", "theme": ["失败与脆弱"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%AB%96%E8%AA%9E/%E8%A1%9E%E9%9D%88%E5%85%AC%E7%AC%AC%E5%8D%81%E4%BA%94?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《论语·卫灵公》15.29", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "daodejing-8", "work": "道德经", "chapter": "第八章", "ref": "8", "original": "上善若水。水善利万物而不争", "gloss": "最高的善像水：滋养万物，却不与人争。", "theme": ["自我与身份", "关系与冲突"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E9%81%93%E5%BE%B7%E7%B6%93_(%E7%8E%8B%E5%BC%BC%E6%9C%AC)?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《道德经》第八章", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "daodejing-22", "work": "道德经", "chapter": "第二十二章", "ref": "22", "original": "夫唯不争，故天下莫能与之争。", "gloss": "正因为不与人争，所以天下没有人能争得过他。", "theme": ["关系与冲突"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E9%81%93%E5%BE%B7%E7%B6%93_(%E7%8E%8B%E5%BC%BC%E6%9C%AC)?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《道德经》第二十二章", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "daodejing-33-1", "work": "道德经", "chapter": "第三十三章", "ref": "33", "original": "知人者智，自知者明。", "gloss": "能看清别人算是聪明，能看清自己才是真正的明白。", "theme": ["自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E9%81%93%E5%BE%B7%E7%B6%93_(%E7%8E%8B%E5%BC%BC%E6%9C%AC)?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《道德经》第三十三章", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "daodejing-33-2", "work": "道德经", "chapter": "第三十三章", "ref": "33", "original": "胜人者有力，自胜者强。", "gloss": "能胜过别人算是有力量，能战胜自己才是真正的强大。", "theme": ["自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E9%81%93%E5%BE%B7%E7%B6%93_(%E7%8E%8B%E5%BC%BC%E6%9C%AC)?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《道德经》第三十三章", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "daodejing-44-1", "work": "道德经", "chapter": "第四十四章", "ref": "44", "original": "名与身孰亲？", "gloss": "名声和生命，哪个更值得亲近？", "theme": ["金钱与安全", "选择与后悔"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E9%81%93%E5%BE%B7%E7%B6%93_(%E7%8E%8B%E5%BC%BC%E6%9C%AC)?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《道德经》第四十四章", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "daodejing-44-2", "work": "道德经", "chapter": "第四十四章", "ref": "44", "original": "知足不辱，知止不殆，可以长久。", "gloss": "知道满足就不会招来屈辱，知道适可而止就不会陷入危险，这样才能长久。", "theme": ["金钱与安全"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E9%81%93%E5%BE%B7%E7%B6%93_(%E7%8E%8B%E5%BC%BC%E6%9C%AC)?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《道德经》第四十四章", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "daodejing-48", "work": "道德经", "chapter": "第四十八章", "ref": "48", "original": "损之又损，以至于无为。无为而无不为。", "gloss": "把执念一减再减，减到不再妄为；不妄为，反而没有什么做不成。", "theme": ["意义与虚无"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E9%81%93%E5%BE%B7%E7%B6%93_(%E7%8E%8B%E5%BC%BC%E6%9C%AC)?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《道德经》第四十八章", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "daodejing-64", "work": "道德经", "chapter": "第六十四章", "ref": "64", "original": "合抱之木，生于毫末；九层之台，起于累土；千里之行，始于足下。", "gloss": "合抱粗的大树从细芽长起，九层的高台从一筐土堆起，千里的远行从脚下第一步开始。", "theme": ["时间与消耗", "失败与脆弱"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E9%81%93%E5%BE%B7%E7%B6%93_(%E7%8E%8B%E5%BC%BC%E6%9C%AC)?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《道德经》第六十四章", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "daodejing-76", "work": "道德经", "chapter": "第七十六章", "ref": "76", "original": "人之生也柔弱，其死也坚强。", "gloss": "人活着的时候身体是柔软的，死了才变得僵硬；刚强往往属于衰亡的一边。", "theme": ["失败与脆弱"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E9%81%93%E5%BE%B7%E7%B6%93_(%E7%8E%8B%E5%BC%BC%E6%9C%AC)?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《道德经》第七十六章", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "daodejing-81", "work": "道德经", "chapter": "第八十一章", "ref": "81", "original": "圣人之道，为而不争。", "gloss": "圣人做事，但不与人争。", "theme": ["关系与冲突", "意义与虚无"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E9%81%93%E5%BE%B7%E7%B6%93_(%E7%8E%8B%E5%BC%BC%E6%9C%AC)?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《道德经》第八十一章", "locator": "", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "zhuangzi-yangshengzhu-1", "work": "庄子", "chapter": "养生主", "ref": "第1段（吾生也有涯）", "original": "吾生也有涯，而知也无涯。以有涯随无涯，殆已。", "gloss": "生命有限，知识却没有尽头；用有限的生命去追逐无限的知识，只会把自己拖垮。", "theme": ["时间与消耗"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%8E%8A%E5%AD%90/%E9%A4%8A%E7%94%9F%E4%B8%BB?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《庄子·养生主》", "locator": "第1段（吾生也有涯）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "zhuangzi-yangshengzhu-2", "work": "庄子", "chapter": "养生主", "ref": "第4段（秦失吊老聃）", "original": "安时而处顺，哀乐不能入也，古者谓是帝之县解。", "gloss": "安于时势、顺应变化，悲哀和快乐就进不到心里；古人把这叫作解开倒悬。", "theme": ["恐惧与焦虑", "失败与脆弱"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%8E%8A%E5%AD%90/%E9%A4%8A%E7%94%9F%E4%B8%BB?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《庄子·养生主》", "locator": "第4段（秦失吊老聃）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "zhuangzi-renjianshi-1", "work": "庄子", "chapter": "人间世", "ref": "第2段（叶公子高将使于齐）", "original": "知其不可奈何而安之若命，德之至也。", "gloss": "知道有些事无可奈何，就把它当作命数安然接受，这是德性最高的地方。", "theme": ["恐惧与焦虑"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%8E%8A%E5%AD%90/%E4%BA%BA%E9%96%93%E4%B8%96?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《庄子·人间世》", "locator": "第2段（叶公子高将使于齐）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "zhuangzi-renjianshi-2", "work": "庄子", "chapter": "人间世", "ref": "第2段（叶公子高将使于齐）", "original": "且夫乘物以游心，托不得已以养中，至矣", "gloss": "顺着外物的变化让心自由游走，把不得已当作养心的凭借，这就够了。", "theme": ["意义与虚无"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%8E%8A%E5%AD%90/%E4%BA%BA%E9%96%93%E4%B8%96?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《庄子·人间世》", "locator": "第2段（叶公子高将使于齐）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "zhuangzi-renjianshi-3", "work": "庄子", "chapter": "人间世", "ref": "第7段（孔子适楚）", "original": "人皆知有用之用，而莫知无用之用也。", "gloss": "人们都知道「有用」的用处，却不知道「无用」也有它的用处。", "theme": ["意义与虚无", "自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%8E%8A%E5%AD%90/%E4%BA%BA%E9%96%93%E4%B8%96?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《庄子·人间世》", "locator": "第7段（孔子适楚）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "zhuangzi-qiwulun-1", "work": "庄子", "chapter": "齐物论", "ref": "第7段（夫道未始有封）", "original": "故知止其所不知，至矣。", "gloss": "知道自己该在哪里停下来、不越过自己所知的边界，这就是最高的智慧。", "theme": ["自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%8E%8A%E5%AD%90/%E9%BD%8A%E7%89%A9%E8%AB%96?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《庄子·齐物论》", "locator": "第7段（夫道未始有封）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "zhuangzi-qiushui-1", "work": "庄子", "chapter": "秋水", "ref": "第1段（北海若答河伯）", "original": "夏虫不可以语于冰者，笃于时也。", "gloss": "夏天的虫子没法跟它谈冰，因为它被时令限制住了——人的见识也常被处境锁住。", "theme": ["关系与冲突", "自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%8E%8A%E5%AD%90/%E7%A7%8B%E6%B0%B4?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《庄子·秋水》", "locator": "第1段（北海若答河伯）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "zhuangzi-qiushui-2", "work": "庄子", "chapter": "秋水", "ref": "第8段（孔子游于匡）", "original": "知穷之有命，知通之有时，临大难而不惧者，圣人之勇也。", "gloss": "知道困窘有命数、通达有时机，面对大难仍不恐惧，这才是圣人的勇敢。", "theme": ["恐惧与焦虑", "失败与脆弱"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%8E%8A%E5%AD%90/%E7%A7%8B%E6%B0%B4?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《庄子·秋水》", "locator": "第8段（孔子游于匡）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "zhuangzi-qiushui-3", "work": "庄子", "chapter": "秋水", "ref": "第4段（河伯问贵贱）", "original": "以道观之，物无贵贱；以物观之，自贵而相贱；以俗观之，贵贱不在己。", "gloss": "从道看，万物没有贵贱；从万物自身看，都觉得自己贵重而轻视别人；从世俗看，贵贱由外人的评价决定。", "theme": ["关系与冲突", "自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%8E%8A%E5%AD%90/%E7%A7%8B%E6%B0%B4?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《庄子·秋水》", "locator": "第4段（河伯问贵贱）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "zhuangzi-shanmu-1", "work": "庄子", "chapter": "山木", "ref": "第5段（孔子问子桑雩）", "original": "且君子之交淡若水，小人之交甘若醴；君子淡以亲，小人甘以绝。", "gloss": "君子之间的交情像水一样清淡，小人之间的交情像甜酒一样浓腻；清淡所以能长久亲近，甜腻所以容易断绝。", "theme": ["关系与冲突"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%8E%8A%E5%AD%90/%E5%B1%B1%E6%9C%A8?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《庄子·山木》", "locator": "第5段（孔子问子桑雩）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "mozi-jianai-shang-1", "work": "墨子", "chapter": "兼爱上", "ref": "第4段", "original": "故天下兼相爱则治，交相恶则乱。", "gloss": "天下人彼此相爱就太平，彼此憎恶就混乱。", "theme": ["关系与冲突"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E5%A2%A8%E5%AD%90/%E5%85%BC%E6%84%9B%E4%B8%8A?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《墨子·兼爱上》", "locator": "第4段", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "mozi-jianai-zhong-1", "work": "墨子", "chapter": "兼爱中", "ref": "第3段（夫爱人者）", "original": "夫爱人者，人必从而爱之；利人者，人必从而利之；恶人者，人必从而恶之；害人者，人必从而害之。", "gloss": "爱别人的人，别人也会爱他；给他人好处的人，别人也会给他好处；憎恶、伤害别人的人，也会被同样对待。", "theme": ["关系与冲突"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E5%A2%A8%E5%AD%90/%E5%85%BC%E6%84%9B%E4%B8%AD?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《墨子·兼爱中》", "locator": "第3段（夫爱人者）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "mozi-jianai-zhong-2", "work": "墨子", "chapter": "兼爱中", "ref": "第2段（以兼相爱交相利之法易之）", "original": "视人之国若视其国，视人之家若视其家，视人之身若视其身。", "gloss": "把别人的国家看得像自己的国家，把别人的家看得像自己的家，把别人的身体看得像自己的身体。", "theme": ["关系与冲突"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E5%A2%A8%E5%AD%90/%E5%85%BC%E6%84%9B%E4%B8%AD?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《墨子·兼爱中》", "locator": "第2段（以兼相爱交相利之法易之）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "mozi-feigong-shang-1", "work": "墨子", "chapter": "非攻上", "ref": "第3段", "original": "今小为非，则知而非之。大为非攻国，则不知非，从而誉之，谓之义。", "gloss": "小的过错知道反对，大规模地攻打别国却不知道反对，反而称赞它、说它是义。", "theme": ["自我与身份", "关系与冲突"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E5%A2%A8%E5%AD%90/%E9%9D%9E%E6%94%BB%E4%B8%8A?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《墨子·非攻上》", "locator": "第3段", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "mozi-feigong-zhong-1", "work": "墨子", "chapter": "非攻中", "ref": "第2段（计其所自胜）", "original": "计其所自胜，无所可用也。计其所得，反不如所丧者之多。", "gloss": "计算一场战争所得的胜利，其实没有什么用处；计算所得到的，反而不如所丧失的多。", "theme": ["金钱与安全", "选择与后悔"], "source_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E5%A2%A8%E5%AD%90/%E9%9D%9E%E6%94%BB%E4%B8%AD?variant=zh-hans", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《墨子·非攻中》", "locator": "第2段（计其所自胜）", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1"}
{"id": "apology-38a", "work": "申辩篇", "chapter": "申辩篇", "ref": "Stephanus 38a", "original": "the unexamined life is not worth living", "gloss": "未经省察的人生，不值得过。", "theme": ["意义与虚无", "自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Apology_(Jowett)", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《申辩篇》", "locator": "Stephanus 38a", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "speaker": "苏格拉底（柏拉图文本中的发言者；Jowett 英译）", "language": "en"}
{"id": "apology-21b", "work": "申辩篇", "chapter": "申辩篇", "ref": "Stephanus 21b", "original": "I know that I have no wisdom, small or great", "gloss": "我知道自己在智慧上并没有什么了不起的地方，无论大的还是小的。", "theme": ["自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Apology_(Jowett)", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《申辩篇》", "locator": "Stephanus 21b", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "speaker": "苏格拉底（柏拉图文本中的发言者；Jowett 英译）", "language": "en"}
{"id": "apology-23b", "work": "申辩篇", "chapter": "申辩篇", "ref": "Stephanus 23b", "original": "He, O men, is the wisest, who, like Socrates, knows that his wisdom is in truth worth nothing.", "gloss": "神的意思是：最智慧的人，就是像苏格拉底这样知道自己那点智慧其实一文不值的人。", "theme": ["自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Apology_(Jowett)", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《申辩篇》", "locator": "Stephanus 23b", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "speaker": "苏格拉底（柏拉图文本中的发言者；Jowett 英译）", "language": "en"}
{"id": "apology-28b", "work": "申辩篇", "chapter": "申辩篇", "ref": "Stephanus 28b", "original": "a man who is good for anything ought not to calculate the chance of living or dying; he ought only to consider whether in doing anything he is doing right or wrong—acting the part of a good man or of a bad.", "gloss": "一个真正有价值的人不该盘算活下来的机会，只该考虑自己做的事是对是错、像个好人还是像个坏人。", "theme": ["恐惧与焦虑", "选择与后悔"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Apology_(Jowett)", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《申辩篇》", "locator": "Stephanus 28b", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "speaker": "苏格拉底（柏拉图文本中的发言者；Jowett 英译）", "language": "en"}
{"id": "apology-29a", "work": "申辩篇", "chapter": "申辩篇", "ref": "Stephanus 29a", "original": "For the fear of death is indeed the pretence of wisdom, and not real wisdom, being a pretence of knowing the unknown; and no one knows whether death, which men in their fear apprehend to be the greatest evil, may not be the greatest good.", "gloss": "怕死其实是假装有智慧：假装自己知道未知的事；可没人知道死是不是最大的好事，尽管人们因恐惧而把它当成最大的坏事。", "theme": ["恐惧与焦虑"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Apology_(Jowett)", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《申辩篇》", "locator": "Stephanus 29a", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "speaker": "苏格拉底（柏拉图文本中的发言者；Jowett 英译）", "language": "en"}
{"id": "apology-29d", "work": "申辩篇", "chapter": "申辩篇", "ref": "Stephanus 29d", "original": "are you not ashamed of heaping up the greatest amount of money and honour and reputation, and caring so little about wisdom and truth and the greatest improvement of the soul", "gloss": "你们不觉得羞耻吗：拼命积攒钱财、荣誉和名声，却很少关心智慧、真理和灵魂的完善。", "theme": ["金钱与安全", "意义与虚无"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Apology_(Jowett)", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《申辩篇》", "locator": "Stephanus 29d", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "speaker": "苏格拉底（柏拉图文本中的发言者；Jowett 英译）", "language": "en"}
{"id": "apology-30b", "work": "申辩篇", "chapter": "申辩篇", "ref": "Stephanus 30b", "original": "I tell you that virtue is not given by money, but that from virtue comes money and every other good of man, public as well as private.", "gloss": "德性不是用钱买来的；相反，钱财和其他一切好处都是从德性来的（无论对公还是对私）。", "theme": ["金钱与安全"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Apology_(Jowett)", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《申辩篇》", "locator": "Stephanus 30b", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "speaker": "苏格拉底（柏拉图文本中的发言者；Jowett 英译）", "language": "en"}
{"id": "apology-30e", "work": "申辩篇", "chapter": "申辩篇", "ref": "Stephanus 30e", "original": "I am the gadfly of the Athenian people, given to them by God, and they will never have another, if they kill me.", "gloss": "我是神送给雅典人的牛虻；如果你们杀了我，就再也找不到第二个了。", "theme": ["意义与虚无", "自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Apology_(Jowett)", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《申辩篇》", "locator": "Stephanus 30e", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "blocked": true, "block_reason": "Jowett 页面边栏概要混入正文，不能作为苏格拉底逐字发言。", "speaker": "苏格拉底（柏拉图文本中的发言者；Jowett 英译）", "language": "en"}
{"id": "apology-41d", "work": "申辩篇", "chapter": "申辩篇", "ref": "Stephanus 41d", "original": "no evil can happen to a good man, either in life or after death.", "gloss": "好人无论生前还是死后，都不会遭遇真正的坏事。", "theme": ["恐惧与焦虑"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Apology_(Jowett)", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《申辩篇》", "locator": "Stephanus 41d", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "speaker": "苏格拉底（柏拉图文本中的发言者；Jowett 英译）", "language": "en"}
{"id": "apology-42a", "work": "申辩篇", "chapter": "申辩篇", "ref": "Stephanus 42a", "original": "The hour of departure has arrived, and we go our ways—I to die, and you to live. Which is better God only knows.", "gloss": "分别的时刻到了：我去死，你们去活；哪条路更好，只有神知道。", "theme": ["意义与虚无"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Apology_(Jowett)", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《申辩篇》", "locator": "Stephanus 42a", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "speaker": "苏格拉底（柏拉图文本中的发言者；Jowett 英译）", "language": "en"}
{"id": "hamlet-1-2-133", "work": "哈姆雷特", "chapter": "第一幕", "ref": "Act I, Scene 2, ll. 133–134", "original": "How weary, stale, flat, and unprofitable\nSeem to me all the uses of this world.", "gloss": "这世上的一切在我眼里都那么疲惫、陈旧、平淡而无益。", "theme": ["意义与虚无", "时间与消耗"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Hamlet_(1917)_Yale/Text/Act_I", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《哈姆雷特》第一幕", "locator": "Act I, Scene 2, ll. 133–134", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "language": "en", "speaker": "哈姆雷特"}
{"id": "hamlet-1-3-68", "work": "哈姆雷特", "chapter": "第一幕", "ref": "Act I, Scene 3, l. 68", "original": "Give every man thine ear, but few thy voice;", "gloss": "多听别人说，少发表自己的意见。", "theme": ["关系与冲突"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Hamlet_(1917)_Yale/Text/Act_I", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《哈姆雷特》第一幕", "locator": "Act I, Scene 3, l. 68", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "language": "en", "speaker": "波洛涅斯"}
{"id": "hamlet-1-3-75", "work": "哈姆雷特", "chapter": "第一幕", "ref": "Act I, Scene 3, l. 75", "original": "Neither a borrower, nor a lender be;", "gloss": "既不要向别人借钱，也不要借钱给别人。", "theme": ["金钱与安全"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Hamlet_(1917)_Yale/Text/Act_I", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《哈姆雷特》第一幕", "locator": "Act I, Scene 3, l. 75", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "language": "en", "speaker": "波洛涅斯"}
{"id": "hamlet-1-3-78", "work": "哈姆雷特", "chapter": "第一幕", "ref": "Act I, Scene 3, l. 78", "original": "This above all: to thine own self be true,", "gloss": "最重要的是：对自己诚实。", "theme": ["自我与身份"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Hamlet_(1917)_Yale/Text/Act_I", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《哈姆雷特》第一幕", "locator": "Act I, Scene 3, l. 78", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "language": "en", "speaker": "波洛涅斯"}
{"id": "hamlet-1-5-166", "work": "哈姆雷特", "chapter": "第一幕", "ref": "Act I, Scene 5, ll. 166–167", "original": "There are more things in heaven and earth, Horatio,\nThan are dreamt of in your philosophy.", "gloss": "天地之间的事，比你的哲学所梦想到的要多得多。", "theme": ["意义与虚无"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Hamlet_(1917)_Yale/Text/Act_I", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《哈姆雷特》第一幕", "locator": "Act I, Scene 5, ll. 166–167", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "language": "en", "speaker": "哈姆雷特"}
{"id": "hamlet-2-2-260", "work": "哈姆雷特", "chapter": "第二幕", "ref": "Act II, Scene 2, ll. 260–261", "original": "nothing either good or bad, but thinking makes it so", "gloss": "事情本身无所谓好坏，是人的想法把它变成了这样。", "theme": ["恐惧与焦虑"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Hamlet_(1917)_Yale/Text/Act_II", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《哈姆雷特》第二幕", "locator": "Act II, Scene 2, ll. 260–261", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "language": "en", "speaker": "哈姆雷特"}
{"id": "hamlet-3-1-56", "work": "哈姆雷特", "chapter": "第三幕", "ref": "Act III, Scene 1, l. 56", "original": "To be, or not to be: that is the question:", "gloss": "活下去还是不活下去，这才是问题所在。", "theme": ["意义与虚无"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Hamlet_(1917)_Yale/Text/Act_III", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《哈姆雷特》第三幕", "locator": "Act III, Scene 1, l. 56", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "language": "en", "speaker": "哈姆雷特"}
{"id": "hamlet-3-1-83", "work": "哈姆雷特", "chapter": "第三幕", "ref": "Act III, Scene 1, l. 83", "original": "Thus conscience does make cowards of us all;", "gloss": "思虑顾虑把我们都变成了胆小鬼。", "theme": ["恐惧与焦虑"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Hamlet_(1917)_Yale/Text/Act_III", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《哈姆雷特》第三幕", "locator": "Act III, Scene 1, l. 83", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "language": "en", "speaker": "哈姆雷特"}
{"id": "hamlet-5-2-10", "work": "哈姆雷特", "chapter": "第五幕", "ref": "Act V, Scene 2, ll. 10–11", "original": "There's a divinity that shapes our ends,\nRough-hew them how we will.", "gloss": "冥冥中自有一种力量在塑造我们的结局，无论我们怎么折腾。", "theme": ["意义与虚无"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Hamlet_(1917)_Yale/Text/Act_V", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《哈姆雷特》第五幕", "locator": "Act V, Scene 2, ll. 10–11", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "language": "en", "speaker": "哈姆雷特"}
{"id": "hamlet-5-2-236", "work": "哈姆雷特", "chapter": "第五幕", "ref": "Act V, Scene 2, l. 236", "original": "the readiness is all.", "gloss": "准备好了，就是一切。", "theme": ["恐惧与焦虑"], "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Hamlet_(1917)_Yale/Text/Act_V", "license": "public-domain", "verified": true, "cite": "《哈姆雷特》第五幕", "locator": "Act V, Scene 2, l. 236", "provenance": "supplied-v0.1", "language": "en", "speaker": "哈姆雷特"}
